+ * The second one still collapses the measurement: if a browser noises every
+ * single `toDataURL()` call, BOTH consecutive top-level calls return the
+ * literal string `"unstable"`, and a naive equality test would score that
+ * browser as perfectly *stable*. That is the exact opposite of the truth.
